  "pbtResults": {
    "1.1 Bug 1 - Vary Header Overwrite exploration test": {
      "status": "passed",
      "failingExample": "Bug 1 exploration test SUCCESSFULLY DETECTED the bug (test failures prove bug exists):\n\n**Counterexample 1** - Multiple existing Vary values:\n- Input: Response with `Vary: Origin, Accept-Language` + gzip compression\n- Expected: Vary header contains \"Origin\", \"Accept-Language\", \"Accept-Encoding\"\n- Actual: Vary header contains ONLY \"Accept-Encoding\"\n- Result: Original cache variation markers lost\n\n**Counterexample 2** - Wildcard Vary:\n- Input: Response with `Vary: *` + gzip compression\n- Expected: Vary header remains \"*\"\n- Actual: Vary header changed to \"Accept-Encoding\"\n- Result: Wildcard semantic destroyed\n\n**Counterexample 3** - Single Vary value:\n- Input: Response with `Vary: Origin` + gzip compression\n- Expected: Vary header contains \"Origin, Accept-Encoding\"\n- Actual: Vary header contains ONLY \"Accept-Encoding\"\n- Result: Single existing Vary value lost\n\n**Root Cause Confirmed**: The encoders are using `headers->add(['Vary' => 'Accept-Encoding'])` which REPLACES the existing Vary header instead of using `setVary('Accept-Encoding', false)` which would APPEND to it.",
      "lastRunTimestamp": 1793445720145
    },
    "1.5 Bug 5 - Partial Response Handling exploration test": {
      "status": "passed",
      "failingExample": "Test failures confirm Bug 5 exists:\n1. HTTP 206 partial response test: Response has Content-Encoding header when it should be false (line 512)\n2. Content-Range with status 200 test: Response has Content-Encoding header when it should be false (line 550)\n3. Byte range accuracy test: Compressed body differs from expected partial content (line 586)\n\nAll three test cases demonstrate that 206 partial responses with Content-Range headers are being compressed when they should be skipped. The compressed body (~gzipped) no longer matches the byte range advertised in the Content-Range header, corrupting the partial response semantics.",
      "lastRunTimestamp": 1793449693661
    },
    "1.6 Bug 6 - Fallback Gating exploration test": {
      "status": "passed",
      "failingExample": "All 3 Bug 6 exploration tests failed as expected on unfixed code:\n\n1. \"should fallback to accepted encoding when algorithm config does not match\"\n   - Failed asserting that false is true (line 631)\n   - Expected: Content-Encoding header with 'gzip'\n   - Actual: No Content-Encoding header (response uncompressed)\n   \n2. \"should use fallback encoding when primary algorithm is not accepted\"\n   - Failed asserting that false is true (line 674)\n   - Expected: Content-Encoding header with 'gzip'\n   - Actual: No Content-Encoding header (response uncompressed)\n   \n3. \"should negotiate from candidate list not single algorithm setting\"\n   - Failed asserting that false is true (line 710)\n   - Expected: Content-Encoding header with 'gzip' or 'zstd'\n   - Actual: No Content-Encoding header (response uncompressed)\n\nThis proves Bug 6 exists: when try_multiple_encodings=true but algorithm config doesn't match client's Accept-Encoding, the system returns uncompressed content even though a fallback encoding is available and accepted by the client.",
      "lastRunTimestamp": 1793450156836
    },
