      "status": "passed",
      "failingExample": "Test 1 (pre-compressed fixture): getLongContent() compresses to 73 bytes with gzencode($content, 9), which is below the min_length threshold of 1024 bytes (config default 2048). The test passes because the size check prevents double compression, not because the Content-Encoding header is detected.\n\nTest 2 (first-candidate): Passed - demonstrates that tests claiming to verify first-candidate selection only accept one encoding, so no selection logic is exercised.\n\nTest 3 (vary-preservation): When compression is applied with gzip, the Vary header only contains \"Accept-Encoding\" and loses the original \"Origin\" value. This demonstrates Bug 1 (Vary header overwrite). Tests that request identity encoding never exercise the encoder's Vary header logic because compression is skipped entirely.",
